  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 112 AM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nNorthwest flow will persist aloft, leading to dry conditions for the \nweek. Following a dry frontal passage Sunday morning, the first half \nof the week has high pressure overhead that will shift eastward \nand turn winds from northerly ahead of the surface high to\nsoutherly behind it. High temperatures will be in the mid 60s \nto low 70s and lows in the 40s overnight. Come Wednesday, there \nis another weak shortwave at upper-levels, which will lead to \nanother frontal passage. The chances for rain following the \npassage are limited to less than 10% by the low moisture content\nwith dewpoints in the 50s at the surface and PWATS of less than\nan inch. Upper level cloud coverage will increase and the winds\nwill shift back to northerly at the surface, but we will remain\ndry. The high temperatures see a trend upward to mid 70s during\nthe day and mid 50s overnight for the later half of the week. \nThis is slightly warmer than normal by 5-10 degrees for this \ntime of year. All in all, this week will be a welcome quiet, dry\nperiod to start October.",
